<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · South Asia</p><h1 class="st-title">Western Ganga dynasty</h1><p class="st-meta">350 CE – 1000 CE (approx.) · capital Talakad</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Ganga kings of southern Karnataka, great patrons of Jainism, whose minister raised the colossal statue of Bahubali at Shravanabelagola.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Western Gangas established themselves in the 4th century in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gangavadi">Gangavadi</a>, the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karnataka">Karnataka</a> plateau, as the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/pallava-dynasty">Pallava dynasty</a>'s power waned. Their early capital was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolar">Kolar</a>, later moved to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talakad">Talakad</a> on the Kaveri. Tradition says the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jainism">Jain</a> teacher Simhanandi helped found the dynasty.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/durvinita">Durvinita</a>, an early king, was a scholar who translated works into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a>. The Gangas often served as allies or feudatories of larger neighbours, the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/chalukyas-of-badami">Chalukyas of Badami</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rashtrakuta-dynasty">Rashtrakuta dynasty</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/butuga-ii">Butuga II</a> fought for the Rashtrakutas against the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chola-empire">Cholas</a>. Their land grants supported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jainism">Jain</a> monasteries and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temples. Around 983 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chavundaraya">Chavundaraya</a>, minister of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rachamalla-iv">Rachamalla IV</a>, commissioned the 17-metre <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gommateshwara-statue">statue of Bahubali</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shravanabelagola">Shravanabelagola</a>, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannada">Kannada</a> literature flourished.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After the fall of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rashtrakuta-dynasty">Rashtrakutas</a> the Gangas lost their protector. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajaraja-i">Rajaraja I</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/chola-empire">Chola Empire</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/talakad">Talakad</a> around 1000, ending Ganga rule; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gangavadi">Gangavadi</a> later passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/hoysala-empire">Hoysala Empire</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/western-ganga-dynasty.jpg" alt="Western Ganga dynasty" width="320" height="376"><figcaption>Image: Mlpkr · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Western-ganga-empire-map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>350 CE – 1000 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Talakad</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Durvinita, Butuga II, Rachamalla IV</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Jainism, Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kannada, Sanskrit</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Western Gangas, Gangas of Talakad</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=western-ganga-dynasty" aria-label="Western Ganga dynasty on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6823 1688 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Western Ganga dynasty lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7143 1944L7097 1795M7143 1944L7097 1795M7143 1944L7187 2016"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7097 1795h0M7097 1795h0M7187 2016h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7143 1944h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7143 1944h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=675&amp;focus=western-ganga-dynasty">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

